# Production web build config — COMMITTED to the repo on purpose.
#
# Vite bakes VITE_* vars in at build time. Putting them here (instead of only in
# the Vercel dashboard) makes every deploy deterministic and independent of
# dashboard state — which is what got the hosted build stuck on the local
# backend. `npm run build:web` runs in production mode, so this file loads.
#
# All three values are SAFE to be public / committed:
#   • VITE_API_BACKEND — just selects the backend ("supabase"); not a secret.
#   • VITE_SUPABASE_URL — your project's public URL.
#   • VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — the "anon"/public key. It is PUBLIC by design and
#     already ships in the browser bundle; access is guarded by Row Level
#     Security, not by hiding this key.
# The only true secret is the service_role key — it is NOT here and never should
# be in any committed file or any VITE_ variable.

VITE_API_BACKEND=supabase
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ymjgkcqnyyltqcapfctr.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6InltamdrY3FueXlsdHFjYXBmY3RyIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODQ0OTE3MDEsImV4cCI6MjEwMDA2NzcwMX0.2xtD_l_09OUDtUkVk6SfJjKroFOJkZpO1HgXRnIdtVc
